# Per-player plan-name sequences

Regress automatic naming so only saved plans of the same kind and player advance a default name.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] `Card plan 2` is proposed only when the selected player already has `Card plan 1`.
- [ ] `Con plan 2` is proposed only when the selected player already has `Con plan 1`.
- [ ] A Constructions plan never advances the Cards sequence, and a Cards plan never advances the Constructions sequence.
- [ ] Plans belonging to another player never advance the selected player's sequence.
- [ ] The first unused positive exact default name is selected within the relevant player/kind collection.
- [ ] Unrelated custom names and cancelled unsaved drafts do not advance a sequence.
- [ ] Existing user-entered names are never rewritten.
- [ ] Unit and UI regression coverage compiles for both kinds and multiple players.
- [ ] Focused UI checks pass on a functioning simulator.

## Scope notes

- This clarifies and supersedes any ambiguous cross-kind reading of REQ-014 and verifies TASK-016's intended behavior.
